<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine gov't says wheat damage still unclear.</title>
<headline>Argentine gov't says wheat damage still unclear.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's government is assessing damage to the wheat crop by storms and hail but will have no estimate of losses before Monday, an official said.</p>
<p>&quot;At this moment we have people in the country evaluating this problem. But we will not have a serious estimate of how much damage there has been until Monday,&quot; Patricio Lamarca, an Agricultural Secretariat advisor, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Lamarca said there were reports of wheat sprouting in the ear and that some of the crop might have lost protein content.</p>
<p>Argentina's main farm lobby warned of serious damage but exporters said that losses had been minor.</p>
</text>
